** Helm built-In Objects - Root Objects (.)
- Objects are passed into a template from template engine
- Objects can be simple, and have just one value or they can contain other objects or functions
- It start with root object and in that we have 6 builtin objects
.Release
.Value
.Chart
.Capabilities
.Template
.File

----------

** Helm Root object demo with Notes.txt
- go to the chart --> open notes.txt using vim and clean it
- and add a comment, in NOTES.txt we add a comment like
  {{/* Root or Dot or Period Object */}}
- and below comment we add the details like
Root Objects: {{ . }}
- Now run - helm install mychart . --dry-run

---------
** Helm release and Chart Objects
.Release Object
 - Contains Helm Release information
 - Example: We can put our K8s deployment name in combination with release name using .Release.Name object
   by accessing it in deployment.yaml helm template
 - Now add the below lines in NOTES.txt

 {{/* Release Object */}}
 Release Name: {{ .Release.Name }}
 Release Namespace: {{ .Release.Namespace }}
 Release IsUpgrade: {{ .Release.IsUpgrade }}
 Release IsInstall: {{ .Release.IsInstall }}
 Release Revision: {{ .Release.Revision }}
 Release Service: {{ .Release.Service }}

 ---------------
 ** Helm Values, Capabilities and Template Objects
 .Values Object
 - Values Object contains values from the values.yaml file and if any user-supplied values 
   (-f or --set) that can be passed to templates.

{{/* Values Object */}}
Replica Count: {{ .Values.replicaCount }}
Image Respository: {{ .Values.image.repository }}
Service Type: {{ .Values.service.type }}

--------------
.Capabilities Object 
- This provides information about what capabilities the kubernetes cluster supports

{{/* Capabilities Object */}}
Kubernetes Cluster Version Major: {{ .Capabilities.KubeVersion.Major }}
Kubernetes Cluster Version Minor: {{ .Capabilities.KubeVersion.Minor }}
Helm Version: {{ .Capabilities.HelmVersion }}
Helm Version Semver: {{ .Capabilities.HelmVersion.Version }}

---------
.Template 
 - Container the information of the template that is being executed

 Template Name: {{ .Template.Name }}
 Template BasePath: {{ .Template.BasePath }}
 
